taff\r\n [/ul]\r\n[li] non-proficient weapons (16) 3 open slots\r\n [ul]\r\n [li] healing\r\n [li] herbalism\r\n [li] spellcraft\r\n [li] religion\r\n [li] reading/writing\r\n [li] ancient history\r\n [li] ancient languages\r\n [/ul]\r\n[li] languages\r\n [ul]\r\n [li] english\r\n [li] latin\r\n [li] greek\r\n [li] common\r\n [/ul]\r\n[li] weapons\r\n [ul]\r\n [li] magical quarterstaff +5 int weapon\r\n [li] speech and telepathy\r\n [li] detect good/evil in a 10' radius\r\n [li] detect invisible objects in a 10' radius\r\n [li] detect gem kind and number in a 5' radius\r\n [li] extraordinary powers - teleportations - 1 time/day, 600lbs. max, casting time 2\r\n [/ul]\r\n[li] items\r\n [ul]\r\n [li] ring of wizardry - doubles 2nd level spells\r\n [li] ring of improved invisible\r\n [li] ring of protection +5/+5\r\n [li] portable hole\r\n [li] amulet of life protection\r\n [li] 2 of healing potion\r\n [li] 1 of 10-100 \r\n [li] 1 of 1-10\r\n [li] 2 of 2-50\r\n [/ul]\r\n[li] tools, equipment, non-magical items\r\n [ul]\r\n [li] 5 of candle\r\n [li] 2 of herbs\r\n [li] 2 of oil flask\r\n [li] 5 of iron spike\r\n [li] 2 of silk 50' rope\r\n [li] 2 of sweet water\r\n [li] 1 of large sack\r\n [li] 1 of water skin\r\n [/ul]\r\n[li] kills, encounters, etc\r\n[li] abilities and information\r\n[/ul]\r\n	2003-11-18 15:51:30.690169+00	2004-12-07 15:55:39.86823+00	1		\N	\N	PUBLIC
26	73	1	Mouse Balls		[p]\r\nJuly 12, 1990\r\n[/p]\r\n[p]\r\nSubject: IBM BALL REPLACEMENT\r\n[/p]\r\n[p]\r\nAbstract:  Mouse Balls Available as FRU (Field Replacement Unit) \r\n[/p]\r\n[p]\r\nMouse balls are now available \r\nas FRU.  Therefore if a mouse fails to operate or should it perform \r\nerratically, it may need a ball replacement. \r\n[/p]\r\n[p]\r\nBecause of the delicate \r\nnature of this procedure, replacement of mouse balls should only be \r\nattempted by properly trained personnel.  Before proceeding, determine \r\nthe type of mouse balls by examining the underside of the mouse. \r\n[/p]\r\n[p]\r\nDomestic balls will be \r\nlarger and harder than foreign balls.  Ball removal procedures \r\ndiffer depending upon manufacturer of the mouse. Foreign balls can be \r\nreplaced using the pop-off method.  Domestic balls are replaced \r\nusing the twist off method. \r\n[/p]\r\n[p]\r\nMouse balls are not usually \r\nstatic sensitive; however, excessive handling can result in sudden discharge.  \r\nUpon completion of ball replacement, the mouse may be used immediately. \r\n[/p]\r\n[p]\r\nIt is recommended that \r\neach replacer have a pair of spare balls for maintaining optimum customer \r\nsatisfaction, and that any customer missing his balls should suspect \r\nlocal personnel of removing these necessary items. \r\n[/p]\r\n[p]\r\nTo re-order, specify one \r\nof the following:\r\n[/p]\r\n[p]\r\nP/N 33F6424 - Domestic Mouse Balls\r\n[/p]\r\n[p]\r\nP/N 33F8461 - Foreign Mouse Balls\r\n[/p]\r\n[p]\r\n \r\n[/p]\r\n[p]\r\n \r\n[/p]\r\n[p]\r\n[link:http://www.strangeplaces.net/weirdthings/mouseballs.html]original document[/link]\r\n[/p]\r\n[p]\r\n \r\n[/p]\r\n	2006-11-02 17:05:10.668192+00	2006-11-05 03:10:08.041067+00	1		\N	\N	PUBLIC
25	\N	1	cheater		<PoLaPaIn> how can i write a webapplictaion to dynamically generate a customized multiplication table?[br]\r\n<jonez> PoLaPaIn, carefully ;)[br]\r\n<PoLaPaIn> humm[br]\r\n<PoLaPaIn> jonez...trying to get it done for 3 days but donno what to do :([br]\r\n<PoLaPaIn> yape[br]\r\n<jonez> ask the teacher/prof/assistant[br]\r\n<PoLaPaIn> it's online class[br]\r\n<PoLaPaIn> and he said search in online[br]\r\n<jonez> "search online" does not mean "get someone on irc to give you the answer"[br]\r\n<PoLaPaIn> i searched in online[br]\r\n<PoLaPaIn> but didn't get any clue[br]\r\n<jonez> are you paying for this class?[br]\r\n<jonez> oh wait.. lemme guess.. this is due tomorrow, right?[br]\r\n<jonez> I am willing to help you with syntax errors, but I will not give you the solution.[br]\r\n<jonez> did this teacher give you any kind of example of what sort of result they want?[br]\r\n<PoLaPaIn> he just gave me an example[br]\r\n<PoLaPaIn> he made that one by himself and showed us the output[br]\r\n<PoLaPaIn> and told us you have to do it like this one[br]\r\n<PoLaPaIn> [link:http://164.58.125.200/WebApps/dynamicTables.aspx]http://164.58.125.200/WebApps/dynamicTables.aspx[/link][br]\r\n<PoLaPaIn> Here is the link[br]\r\n<PoLaPaIn> and he didn't say anything told us to search in online to get the multipication code[br]\r\n<jonez> so this teacher gave you permission to use whatever language you want on whatever platform you want?[br]\r\n<jonez> seems kind of unlikely.[br]\r\n<PoLaPaIn> yea[br]\r\n<p0windah> PoLaPaIn: looks tricky[br]\r\n<PoLaPaIn> it doesn't matter to him...as long as the work is done[br]\r\n<p0windah> PoLaPaIn: bleh, just write it in JS[br]\r\n<PoLaPaIn> Java don't have any idea about web developing software[br]\r\n<PoLaPaIn> took that class bcz i have to take a lower label class[br]\r\n<p0windah> PoLaPaIn: you're babbling[br]\r\n<PoLaPaIn> so took it[br]\r\n<PoLaPaIn> i donno.....[br]\r\n<p0windah> PoLaPaIn: anyway, its easy(in the extreme) and pr